**c) `normalizeTelephone` (`:293-308`)** — converts to E.164. Strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps leading `+` and country code, else assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`. Result must match `[0-9]{8,15}` else throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["telephone"])` (→ 400). Stored value is `"+" + digits`.

**d) `normalizeEmail` (`:334-343`)** — null passes through; otherwise trims, must match `EMAIL_PATTERN = ^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$` (`:67`) else throws `InvalidOwnerFieldsException(["email"])` (→ 400); stored **lower-cased**.

**e) registrationDate default (`:121-123`)** — if null, set to `LocalDate.now()` (today = 2026-08-14 per env).

**f) `rejectDuplicateTelephone` (`:353-363`)** — loads **all** owners (`clinicService.findAllOwners()`), normalizes each existing telephone to E.164 (`toE164OrNull`, `:317-323`), and if any equals the new one throws `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` (→ 409).

**g) `rejectDuplicateHousehold` (`:375-384`)** — skipped when `sharesHousehold == true`. Otherwise compares lastName+address case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace (`normalizeForComparison`, `:394-399`) against all owners; match throws `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` (→ 409).

**h) `nextCustomerCode` (`:239-244`)** — assigns `customerCode` formatted `"<LAST3>-<NNNN>"`: upper-cased first 3 letters of last name + zero-padded `(findAllOwners().size() + 1)`. E.g. `SMI-0011`.

**i) `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`:129`)** — persists (section 5).

**j)** Response: maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, returns **201 CREATED**.

No password encoding, no events published, no auditing side-effects in this flow (password encoding exists only for Users, not Owners).

