## 5. Service layer + repository save

**Service** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:232-237`
```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);

}
```
It is a thin `@Transactional` pass-through — no validation, uniqueness checks, transformations, defaults, or events. (Interface: `ClinicService.saveOwner`.)

**Repository** — interface `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java:66` declares `void save(Owner owner)`.

Active profile is `h2,spring-data-jpa` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/application.properties:20`), so the implementation is **Spring Data's generated proxy** for `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java:36-37` (`@Profile("spring-data-jpa")`, extends `Repository<Owner, Integer>`). `save` is not custom-overridden there — Spring Data does `persist` for a new entity (null id) / `merge` otherwise.

For reference, the `@Profile("jpa")` alternative implements save explicitly — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java:92-100`:
```java
@Override
public void save(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getId() == null) {
        this.em.persist(owner);
    } else {
        this.em.merge(owner);
    }
}
```

**JPA lifecycle callbacks: NONE.** A search for `@PrePersist/@PreUpdate/@PostPersist/@EntityListeners/auditing` across `src` returned zero hits. `Owner` → `Person` (`@MappedSuperclass`) → `BaseEntity` (`@MappedSuperclass`, `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java`) — `BaseEntity` only defines `@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)`. No callback hooks anywhere. Any `customerCode`/`registrationDate` defaulting is done in the controller, not via lifecycle hooks.

